<ContentPage
  title="About SpedCentral | Our Mission & Story"
  description="SpedCentral connects Houston families with verified special education providers, specialists, and products -- built by people who believe finding the right support shouldn't be this hard."
  heading="About SpedCentral"
>
  <h2>Why we started SpedCentral</h2>
  <p>
    Finding the right speech therapist, ABA provider, or dyslexia tutor for your child usually means digging through
    scattered directories, insurance portals, and word-of-mouth referrals -- often while you're already stretched
    thin. SpedCentral exists to put that search in one place: verified special education providers, specialists,
    and the products that support them, organized the way families actually search, not the way clinics happen to
    be organized internally.
  </p>
  <p>
    We started in Houston, Texas, because it's a large, diverse metro with no shortage of great providers -- just no
    single place to find them. Our plan is to bring the same directory to every U.S. metro, and eventually beyond
    the U.S., without ever losing the thing that makes it useful: every listing is a real, reviewed provider, not
    an unmoderated ad.
  </p>

  <h2>What we do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Provider directory</strong> -- speech-language pathologists, occupational and physical therapists, ABA/behavioral therapists, dyslexia and reading specialists, advocates, attorneys, and more, all reviewed before they're listed.</li>
    <li><strong>Product catalog</strong> -- sensory tools, assistive technology, adaptive classroom supplies, and daily-living aids, organized by what they're actually used for.</li>
    <li><strong>Guides &amp; resources</strong> -- plain-language answers to the questions that come up most for families navigating IEPs, evaluations, and therapy options.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How we make money</h2>
  <p>
    SpedCentral is free for families to use. Providers can list for free; some choose to pay for featured
    placement, which we always label clearly as "Sponsored" -- it never replaces our credential review, and it
    never means a lower-rated provider outranks a better one in search results outside the featured section. Some
    product links are affiliate links, disclosed on our <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">Affiliate Disclosure</a>
    page.
  </p>

  <h2>Where we are today</h2>
  <p>
    SpedCentral is new and growing. We're starting deep in one metro -- Houston -- rather than spreading thin
    across the country on day one, because a directory with real, vetted listings in one city is more useful than
    an empty one covering fifty states. If you don't see your specialty or city yet, <a href="/contact/">let us know</a> --
    we're adding new providers and categories every week.
  </p>
</ContentPage>
